==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|sharply}}, {{m|enm|scharply}}, from {{inh|en|ang|sċearplīċe|t=sharply, smartly}}, equivalent to {{af|en|sharp|-ly}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈʃɑɹpli/|a=GA}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈʃɑːpli/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-sharply.ogg|a=US}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|er|more}}

# In a [[sharp]] manner, in various senses.
## So as to terminate in a sharp [[point]] or [[edge]].
##: {{ux|en|The stick was '''sharply''' tapered at one end.}}
## [[rapidly|Rapidly]], [[abruptly]].
##: {{ux|en|When I touched the snake it recoiled '''sharply'''.}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|date=June 18 2013|author=w:Simon Romero|title=Protests Widen as Brazilians Chide Leaders|titleurl=http://www.nytimes.com/2013/06/19/world/americas/brazilian-leaders-brace-for-more-protests.html|journal=New York Times|accessdate=21 June 2013
|passage=The economy has slowed to a pale shadow of its growth in recent years; inflation is high, the currency is declining '''sharply''' against the dollar — but the expectations of Brazilians have rarely been higher, feeding broad intolerance with corruption, bad schools and other government failings.}}
## {{lb|en|to describe breathing}} Suddenly and intensely like a [[gasp]], but typically as the result of an emotional reaction.
## [[precisely|Precisely]], [[accurately]].
##: {{ux|en|a '''sharply''' focused essay}}
## [[quickly|Quickly]] and [[alertly]].
##: {{ux|en|Jones, the centre forward, started the game '''sharply'''.}}
##* {{quote-journal|en
|date=November 11, 2011
|author=Rory Houston
|title=Estonia 0-4 Republic of Ireland
|work=RTE Sport
|url=http://www.rte.ie/sport/soccer/2011/1111/estonia_ireland_report.html
|page=
|passage=Walters tried a long range shot in the third minute as he opened the game '''sharply''', linking well with Robbie Keane, but goalkeeper Sergei Pareiko gathered the ball with ease.}}
## Of speech, [[sternly]], [[harshly]] or [[critically]].
##: {{ux|en|When I asked her about her husband, she replied '''sharply''' that she had not seen him for several months.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Johanna Spyri
|by=Eileen Hall
|title=Heidi
|year=1956
|origyear=1880
|page=99
|passage=Before long Tinette stuck her head round the door, and said '''sharply''', 'You're to go to the study.'}}
## [[stylishly|Stylishly]], [[smartly]].
##: {{ux|en|He was '''sharply''' dressed in an expensive suit.}}
## So as to form a sharp, or tight, angle.
##: {{ux|en|Turn '''sharply''' to the right.}}
## [[steeply|Steeply]]; [[precipitously]].
##: {{ux|en|The road descends '''sharply'''.}}
## [[piercing|Piercingly]]; [[keenly]]; [[severely]]; [[painfully]].
##: {{ux|en|His old war wound twinged '''sharply'''.}}
## In an [[intellectual]]ly [[alert]] and [[penetrating]] manner.
##* {{RQ:Travers Cuckoo in the Nest|chapter=1|passage=Peter, after the manner of man at the breakfast table, had allowed half his kedgeree to get cold and was sniggering over a letter. Sophia looked at him '''sharply'''. The only letter she had received was from her mother. Sophia's mother was not a humourist.}}
## In a strongly distinguishing or differentiating manner; [[acutely]].
##: {{ux|en|The wealth of this small country contrasts '''sharply''' with that of its neighbours.}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|date=2023 November 15|author=Paul Clifton|title=Early responses to Scottish fares trial|journal=RAIL|issue=996|pages=44-45|text=Hynes is careful to direct the credit to his paymasters in the Scottish Government, whose ambitions for rail contrast increasingly '''sharply''' with those in Westminster.}}

